# FUTURE: nice-to-have follow-ups (`@meridian/thread-client`)

- Hand-back chips are inferred, not exact. The stored message keeps only a
  reference's document and URI, so `chatReferenceResolver`
  (`src/message/hand-back.ts`) rebuilds a chip only when the URI proves the
  owner, and returns link text otherwise: a reference to another named Work
  comes back as text, and an extension-less document of a non-markdown type
  gets a markdown chip (an image block in the message still makes an image
  chip). No content is lost. The exact fix keeps the chip's `fileType` and
  owner (`RestorableReference`) in the send contract
  (`packages/contracts/src/protocol/user-turn-admission.ts`, the message
  builder in `src/message/`, and the server's stored occurrence), so the
  inverse reads them instead of inferring.
